{"diagnosis": "Loopback test programs divider 64 then sends 0xa5 but traps on uart timeout with no byte received, so recv_buf_valid never asserted. Expected cfg_divider=64 but byte-0 write uses cfg_divider[ 7: 1] <= reg_div_di[ 7: 0], truncating the LSB and leaving bit0 stale. This mis-programmed divider in the excerpt breaks TX/RX bit timing so the loopback byte is never sampled.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@
 		if (!resetn) begin
 			cfg_divider <= DEFAULT_DIV;
 		end else begin
-			if (reg_div_we[0]) cfg_divider[ 7: 1] <= reg_div_di[ 7: 0];
+			if (reg_div_we[0]) cfg_divider[ 7: 0] <= reg_div_di[ 7: 0];
 			if (reg_div_we[1]) cfg_divider[15: 8] <= reg_div_di[15: 8];
 			if (reg_div_we[2]) cfg_divider[23:16] <= reg_div_di[23:16];
 			if (reg_div_we[3]) cfg_divider[31:24] <= reg_div_di[31:24];", "expected": "tohost PASS with loopback 0xa5 received, no uart timeout"}

